  "$comment": "The corpus's own citation labels for every hadith address the Golden Set and the matn-identity map name, read from the immutable raw editions the ingest aligns (hadith/ara-*.json and hadith/ind-*.json under the corpus root, fawazahmed0/hadith-api, Unlicense). The label is the comparison form the citation gate builds (collection name folded, grade suffix stripped); collection, hadithNo and grade are the row's own fields, so a curated label that is absent here names no corpus row. An address enters this file only after its row was read in the raw editions and matched to its Indonesian counterpart; the test cannot re-read the corpus, so the pinned entry is the curator's verification. Not gate data: it widens nothing.",
